# Visor — 1.5.4

## Visor Studio companion

- The official visual `boot.conf` configurator, [Visor Studio](https://github.com/Versedcamel153/visor-studio), is now a first-class companion, documented in the README and wired into both the CLI and the installer. Built by [@Versedcamel153](https://github.com/Versedcamel153) (Farid).
- New `visor studio` command — clones, updates (`--update`), and launches the configurator on `http://127.0.0.1:8000` (`--port PORT`). Uses Docker when available (single `visor-studio` container), otherwise builds a python3 venv + Vite frontend. `--docker` forces the Docker path; `--detach` runs it in the background.
- `install.sh` now pre-fetches Visor Studio during install so it runs offline: a `--studio`/`--no-studio` flag (or an interactive prompt) clones the companion into the host cache (`~/.cache/visor-studio`), resolving the real user's home under `sudo` and handing ownership back. The `visor studio` command finds the same checkout.

## Tooling fixes (over-mounted ESPs)

- `install.sh` and the `visor` CLI no longer mis-detect over-mounted ESPs: `findmnt -U` (unique) ignores bind/over-mounts, so the EFI System Partition, its device, and the boot-filesystem type are resolved correctly.

## `visor status` on unreadable ESPs

- `visor status` reports cleanly when the ESP isn't readable (no sudo): it prints `unreadable` for the installed binary, config and boot log, `unknown` for the UEFI entry and sha256 instead of failing cryptically, and hints to re-run with `sudo`.

## `visor clean --all`

- `visor clean` gained `--all`, which also removes the cached `~/.cache/visor` source checkout (and the legacy `~/.cache/visor-src` path) with per-directory confirmation, then reminds you to `visor update` to re-clone.

